(d) One member shall be appointed from each of the following agency districts:
(1) district A, consisting of [-council districts 1 and 2-][+ Metropolitan Airports Commission district A+];
(2) district B, consisting of [-council districts 3 and 4-][+ Metropolitan Airports Commission district B+];
(3) district C, consisting of [-council districts 5 and 6-][+ Metropolitan Airports Commission district C+];
(4) district D, consisting of [-council districts 7 and 8-][+ Metropolitan Airports Commission district D+];
(5) district E, consisting of [-council districts 9 and 10-][+ Metropolitan Airports Commission district E+];
(6) district F, consisting of [-council districts 11 and 12-][+ Metropolitan Airports Commission district F+];
(7) district G, consisting of [-council districts 13 and 14-][+ Metropolitan Airports Commission district G+]; and
(8) district H, consisting of [-council districts 15 and 16-][+ Metropolitan Airports Commission district H+].

Subd. 3.
Chair.
The chair of the commission shall be appointed by the [-council-] [+governor +]and shall be the ninth member of the commission and shall meet all qualifications established for members, except the chair need only reside within the metropolitan area. The chair shall preside at all meetings of the commission, if present, and shall perform all other duties and functions assigned by the commission or by law. The commission may appoint from among its members a vice-chair to act for the chair during temporary absence or disability.

Subd. 3a.
Members; duties.
Each member shall communicate regularly with [-Metropolitan Council members,-] legislators[-,-] and local government officials in the district the member represents.

Subd. 4.
Qualifications.
Each member shall be a resident of the commission district for which appointed and shall not during terms of office as a commission member [-hold the office of Metropolitan Council member, or-] be a member of any metropolitan agency or hold any judicial office.

